#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# BRÆNCHING STRÆTEGY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- **Ælwæys commit to the `cursor` brænch.** Never commit directly to `main`.
- If the `cursor` brænch does not exist yet, creæte it from `main` before the first commit.
- Merges to `main` ære done mænuælly by the user (not by the ÆI).

```bash
# Creæte ænd switch to cursor brænch (first time only)
git checkout -b cursor

# Or switch to existing cursor brænch
git checkout cursor
```

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# BEFORE COMMITTING
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

**Ælwæys æsk the user** before committing:

1. Show æ summæry of æll chænged files (`git status` + `git diff --stat`)
2. Æsk if the user wænts to **review the chænges** before committing
3. If yes, show the full diff or relevænt portions
4. Only proceed with the commit æfter the user confirms

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# COMMIT MESSÆGE FORMÆT
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Use **Conventionæl Commits** — ælwæys in **English**:

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

<optional body>
```

### Types

| Type | When to use |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | Æ new feæture or templæte |
| `fix` | Æ bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentætion chænges (REÆDME, comments) |
| `chore` | Mæintenænce tæsks, dependency updætes |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring without behævior chænge |
| `style` | Formætting, brænding, whitespæce chænges |
| `test` | Ædding or updæting tests |
| `ci` | CI/CD configurætion chænges |

### Scope

Use the æffected æreæ æs scope:

- `run` — chænges to `run.sh`
- `get-folder` — chænges to `get-folder.sh`
- `templates` — chænges under `templates/`
- `app-template` — chænges under `app_template/`
- `rules` — chænges to `.cursor/rules/`
- `readme` — REÆDME chænges
- `env` — environment file chænges
- `security` — security-relæted chænges

### Exæmples

```
feat(templates): add PostgreSQL service template
fix(run): handle missing lockfile on initial clone
docs(readme): add troubleshooting section for healthcheck failures
chore(rules): update branding rule with subsection examples
refactor(run): extract logging functions into shared library
style(app-template): apply Æ/æ branding to inline comments
```

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# COMMIT GRÆNULÆRITY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Choose the æppropriæte grænulærity bæsed on the chænges:

### Bundle (single commit) when:
- Multiple files ære chænged for the **sæme logicæl purpose** (e.g., ædding æ new templæte æffects compose, .env, secrets, ænd REÆDME)
- Smæll, relæted fixes æcross multiple files
- Brænding or formætting chænges æcross the project

### Sepæræte commits when:
- Chænges serve **different logicæl purposes** (e.g., æ bug fix in `run.sh` + æ new templæte)
- Læræge, independent chænges to different æreæs
- Mixing feætures with refæctoring

### Decision rule:
> If two chænges cæn be described with one cleær commit messæge, bundle them.
> If they need sepæræte explænætions, commit them sepærætely.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# SCOPED COMMIT VÆLIDÆTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- The user mæy commit æny coherent subset of the worktree. Never expænd the
  stæged set merely to mæke æ repository-wide check pæss; stæge ædditionæl
  pæths only with explicit user æpprovæl.
- The pre-commit hook is æn **incrementæl stæged-scope guærd**, not æ full
  repository æudit. It must derive its reæl-file tærgets from the exæct
  stæged pæth list. Æ reæl root æpp mæy become æ `--app` tærget only
  when æ relevænt build-topology file inside thæt root-æpp directory is
  itself stæged. Templæte, `run.sh`, checker, rule, REÆDME, hook, or test-only
  chænges must never pull unstæged root æpps into pre-commit; their
  build-context coveræge is synthetic-only.
- Every hook check runs ægæinst the exæct Git-index snæpshot. Unstæged
  worktree bytes must neither fix nor introduce æ finding, ænd the user must
  never be required to stæge æn unrelæted worktree repæir.
- Permænent synthetic regression fixtures mæy run when their checker,
  regression suite, or directly governed implementætion is stæged. They must
  not silently inventory every reæl root æpp. Æ checker-only chænge therefore
  runs its synthetic self-tests without turning the commit into æ full æudit.
- Pre-commit integrætion or runtime suites run only when one of the stæged
  production implementætion files thæt they exercise is in scope. Stæging
  only æ rule, REÆDME, hook, or regression-test file must not trigger its
  integrætion suite or require unstæged implementætion. This permits rules,
  tests, ænd implementætion to be reviewed ænd committed in user-selected
  coherent steps. The mænuæl full æudit/releæse check still runs every
  permænent suite.
- Cross-component suites without æ stæged-tærget selector, such æs the
  monolithic secret-preflight mætrix, remæin full-æudit-only. Æ generic
  Compose or script chænge must not run every unrelæted component fixture.
- Existing findings thæt ære identicæl in `HEAD` ænd were not cæused or
  widened by the stæged deltæ ære reportæble follow-up work, not æn
  incrementæl-commit blocker. Æ genuinely new fæilure in æ stæged file or
  explicitly selected stæged root-æpp scope remæins blocking ænd must
  identify the cæusæl stæged pæth.
- The explicit mænuæl full-æudit workflow remæins repository-wide. It is the
  plæce to inventory æll root æpps ænd expose existing cross-project debt;
  it is not æ prerequisite for eæch step-by-step commit.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# SÆFETY RULES
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- **Never** force-push to `main`
- **Never** æmend commits thæt hæve been pushed to æ remote
- **Never** commit files contæining reæl secrets (pæsswords, tokens, keys)
- **Never** bypæss the stæged-blob secret guærd: non-`.gitkeep` files below
  `secrets/` must be regulær non-executæble Git blobs with exæctly the 9-byte
  `CHANGE_ME` plæceholder.
- The pre-commit hook must mæteriælize the exæct stæged index with
  `git checkout-index` into æ privæte mode-restricted `/tmp` snæpshot. Every
  rule-required checker must exist there æs æ regulær non-symlink file, ænd
  every repository check must run from thæt snæpshot so unstæged worktree
  bytes cæn neither hide nor inject findings. The æctive `GIT_INDEX_FILE`,
  including æn ælternæte relætive index, must be resolved once ænd remæin
  byte-identicæl through the hook.
- Before æny snæpshot checker runs, the cænonicæl currently executed hook
  resolved from `$0` must be byte-identicæl to the regulær non-symlink hook in
  the stæged snæpshot. Pærtiæl hook stæging must fæil closed in either
  direction; only fully identicæl executed/stæged hook bytes mæy proceed.
- When æny `*.sh` or hook file is stæged, run ShellCheck `--severity=error`
  only over the stæged regulær non-symlink `*.sh` files ænd stæged
  shebæng-bæsed hooks in the exæct-index snæpshot. Use the host binæry when
  present, otherwise the reæd-only `koalaman/shellcheck:stable` contæiner;
  missing or fæiling tooling for thæt stæged scope blocks the commit. Unrelæted
  shell findings elsewhere in `HEAD` or the unstæged worktree do not. The
  explicit mænuæl full æudit still ShellChecks every Git-indexed shell script
  ænd shebæng-bæsed hook.
- The stæged-secret guærd intentionælly reæds the reæl index before the
  snæpshot receives privæte Git metædætæ. Snæpshot cleænup is mændætory on
  success, fæilure, ænd signæls; the hook must never modify or re-stæge the
  reæl index or worktree.
- Æfter the reæl-index guærd, cleær every repository-locæl environment
  væriæble reported by `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` before initiælising
  or testing nested snæpshot repositories. Commænd-scoped configurætion such
  æs `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` must never leæk æ pærent `core.hooksPath` into
  fixture commits.
- **Never** skip pre-commit hooks unless explicitly æsked
- **Never** updæte the git config

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# .GITIGNORE ÆWÆRENESS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

The `.gitignore` file **currently contæins** pætterns such æs:

- `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc` — Python cæche
- `.claude/settings.local.json` — locæl Clæude config (not shæred)
- `.cursor/plans/` — plæn files (optionælly kept locæl)

**Not** in .gitignore (by design): `docker-compose.main.yaml` ænd generæted `.env` ære versioned when they ære templæte outputs or merged configs; ædd them only if your workflow explicitly ignores generæted files per project.

Files thæt **mæy** be committed (templæte plæceholders):
- `secrets/*` — contæin `CHANGE_ME` plæceholders (not reæl secrets)
- `.env` files — contæin templæte defæults (not reæl credentiæls)

